  "body": "## Pulse Music v3.2.5 - Startup Stability, PulseMusicActivity Branding & Windows Desktop Update\n\n### ≡ƒÜÇ Startup Stability & Exception Elimination\n- **Resolved NullPointerException in SharedViewModel**: Reordered property initialization sequence so that `_lyricsVoteState`, `_translatedVoteState`, and updater state flows are strictly initialized before `init` coroutines launch.\n- **Defensive Guard on Lyrics Vote Reset**: Wrapped `resetLyricsVoteState()` with fault-tolerant execution, preventing race condition crashes when resuming playback on Android 16 (SDK 36) devices.\n- **Protected Background Retrieval**: Safeguarded `getLyricsFromFormat` against null reference propagation.\n\n### ≡ƒô▒ Pulse Music Activity Renaming\n- **Replaced MainActivity with PulseMusicActivity**: Migrated main entry point from `MainActivity.kt` to `PulseMusicActivity.kt` for cohesive, authentic Pulse Music application branding.\n- **Seamless Home Shortcut Compatibility**: Added `<activity-alias>` in `AndroidManifest.xml` targeting `PulseMusicActivity` to maintain existing launcher widgets and shortcuts without user friction.\n- **Logging & Crash Reporting Alignment**: Updated logging tags and activity tracking to `PulseMusicActivity`.\n\n### ≡ƒûÑ∩╕Å Windows Desktop Package Overhaul (v3.2.5)\n- **Resolved v3.1.7 Stale Version Bug**: Rebuilt native Windows x64 binaries directly from the latest Compose Multiplatform 2026 toolchain. Windows client now correctly runs and displays `v3.2.5`.\n- **MSI Installer & Portable Zip**: Provides both official Windows Installer (`PulseMusic-Windows-x64-Setup.msi`) and standalone portable archive (`PulseMusic-Windows-x64-Setup.zip`).\n\n### ≡ƒÅ¬ Multi-Store & OTA Synchronization\n- **Orion Store Integration**: Synchronized release metadata for warehouse submission (#1819) with `apk` keyword detection.\n- **F-Droid & Obtainium**: Updated fastlane changelog metadata (build `93`) and F-Droid package schema.\n- **Dynamic CDN Cache Purge**: Continuous multi-endpoint arbitration delivering instant update detection.\n"
